{"parentUuid":"d18d379d-5ed7-4218-874e-8b5e21144d7a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KuxCcEpzVeC1RHQ8S1H259","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B6gznvXk4vMDq7iUQh9yGX","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"SoCG 2025 maximum empty rectangle packing optimality"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7286,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":320,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7286},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7286,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy63r1Kxf2Hu6FKbyt3","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed7fe978-6de8-4175-8da1-d3f88f3ef26e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:00.560Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0cd2ca97-393f-4b7d-9859-6dc02474b4ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HSxaK1equAkyPTRBCZW2oR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"maximum empty rectangle algorithm Naamad Lee Hsu 1984 computational geometry\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Largest empty rectangle - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largest_empty_rectangle\"},{\"title\":\"On the maximum empty rectangle problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0166218X84901240\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes Timothy M. Chan !\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol189-socg2021/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fast algorithms for computing the largest empty rectangle | Proceedings of the third annual symposium on Computational geometry\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/41958.41988\"},{\"title\":\"A Note on Finding a Maximum Empty Rectangle\",\"url\":\"https://docs.lib.purdue.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1409&context=cstech\"},{\"title\":\"Computing a Largest Empty Arbitrary Oriented Rectangle: Theory and Implementation | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/3-540-44842-X_81\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes Timothy M. Chan∗\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.08043\"},{\"title\":\"maxempty: Maximally Empty Rectangle Problem in adagio: Discrete and Global Optimization Routines\",\"url\":\"https://rdrr.io/rforge/adagio/man/maxempty.html\"},{\"title\":\"A new algorithm for the largest empty rectangle problem | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01840377\"},{\"title\":\"Largest empty rectangle - HandWiki\",\"url\":\"https://handwiki.org/wiki/Largest_empty_rectangle\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the maximum empty rectangle algorithm by Naamad, Lee, and Hsu:\n\n## The Problem\n\nA problem first discussed by Naamad, Lee and Hsu in 1983 is stated as follows: given a rectangle A containing n points, find a largest-area rectangle with sides parallel to those of A which lies within A and does not contain any of the given points.\n\n## The Algorithm\n\nThe maximum empty rectangle problem involves finding a maximum area rectangle that is fully contained in A and does not contain any point of S in its interior. An O(n²) time algorithm is presented. Additionally, if the points of S are drawn randomly and independently from A, the problem can be solved in O(n(log n)²) expected time.\n\n## Historical Significance\n\nThe earliest reference on the 2D problem appears to be by Naamad, Lee, and Hsu in 1984, who gave a quadratic-time algorithm. In 1986, Chazelle, Drysdale, and Lee obtained an O(n log³ n)-time algorithm. Subsequently, at SoCG'87, Aggarwal and Suri presented another algorithm requiring O(n log³ n) time, followed by a more complicated second algorithm requiring O(n log² n) time.\n\nThe paper was published in *Discrete Applied Mathematics*, Volume 8, Issue 3, July 1984, pages 267-277, and remains a foundational work in computational geometry.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"49692185-9477-4493-956e-6d63c93cd0e7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:05.575Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cd2ca97-393f-4b7d-9859-6dc02474b4ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ed7fe978-6de8-4175-8da1-d3f88f3ef26e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6gznvXk4vMDq7iUQh9yGX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SoCG 2025 maximum empty rectangle packing optimality\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0557\"},{\"title\":\"On three soft rectangle packing problems with guillotine constraints | Journal of Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10898-019-00741-w\"},{\"title\":\"Improved Approximation Algorithms for Three-Dimensional Knapsack\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol332-socg2025/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.60/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.60.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Anchored Rectangle and Square Packings\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2016.13\"},{\"title\":\"Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/260039071_Optimal_Rectangle_Packing_An_Absolute_Placement_Approach\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: Initial Results Richard E. Korf\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.aaai.org/ICAPS/2003/ICAPS03-029.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[1402.0557] Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1402.0557\"},{\"title\":\"Packing problems - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Packing_problems\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement Approach | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Optimal-Rectangle-Packing:-An-Absolute-Placement-Huang-Korf/2331ce6d040864872513b2cefc615606efb6169f\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found one SoCG 2025 paper related to packing problems, but it focuses on three-dimensional knapsack rather than maximum empty rectangle packing specifically.\n\nThe search returned a SoCG 2025 paper on improved approximation algorithms for three-dimensional knapsack, which obtains (139/29 + ε)-approximation for 3DK and (30/7 + ε)-approximation for 3DKR (when rotations by 90 degrees are allowed around all axes).\n\nHowever, this paper does not specifically address \"maximum empty rectangle packing optimality\" as described in your query. The search results primarily returned papers on general rectangle packing optimization, optimal rectangle packing approaches, and other packing-related problems, but no papers specifically focused on maximum empty rectangle packing optimality at SoCG 2025.\n\nIf you're looking for a specific SoCG 2025 paper on maximum empty rectangle packing optimality, you may want to:\n- Check the full SoCG 2025 conference proceedings directly\n- Search with different keywords related to the specific problem variant\n- Provide more details about the paper's authors or specific problem formulation\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3ce3509a-b924-4672-b057-a07e3a75d8d2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:05.619Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed7fe978-6de8-4175-8da1-d3f88f3ef26e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"62e6bbaa-ad7d-48e8-8ac7-0d7d0216487f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbkDHQa7kZtTXBeioTzctV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Aggarwal Suri 1987 maximum empty rectangle optimal algorithm\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Fast algorithms for computing the largest empty rectangle | Proceedings of the third annual symposium on Computational geometry\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/41958.41988\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes Timothy M. Chan !\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol189-socg2021/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Computing a Largest Empty Arbitrary Oriented Rectangle: Theory and Implementation | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/3-540-44842-X_81\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes | Discrete & Computational Geometry | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00454-022-00473-x\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes Timothy M. Chan∗\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.08043\"},{\"title\":\"Fast Algorithms for Computing the Largest Empty Rectangle lEeemiaiA~~\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/41958.41988\"},{\"title\":\"Fast parallel algorithms for the Maximum Empty Rectangle problem | Sādhanā | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF02811344\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/350087384_Faster_Algorithms_for_Largest_Empty_Rectangles_and_Boxes\"},{\"title\":\"Fast parallel algorithms for the Maximum Empty Rectangle ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ias.ac.in/article/fulltext/sadh/017/01/0221-0236\"},{\"title\":\"On the maximum empty hyper-rectangle problem - Rewayda Razaq Abo-Alsabeh, Hajem Ati Daham, Abdellah Salhi, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/17483026221151197\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about the Aggarwal and Suri 1987 paper on maximum empty rectangle algorithms:\n\n## Aggarwal & Suri 1987 - Fast Algorithms for Computing the Largest Empty Rectangle\n\nThe paper by A. Aggarwal and S. Suri addresses the problem of computing the largest-area and largest-perimeter subrectangles with sides parallel to a given rectangle that lie within that rectangle and do not contain any points in their interior.\n\n### Algorithm Complexity\n\nThe paper presented two algorithms for finding the largest-area empty rectangle, with the second algorithm being more complicated but taking only O(n log² n) time and O(n) memory space.\n\nThe first algorithm takes O(n log³ n) time and O(n) memory space and simplifies the algorithm given by Chazelle, Drysdale and Lee which takes O(n log³ n) time but O(n log n) storage.\n\n### Significance\n\nAt SoCG'87, Aggarwal and Suri presented an algorithm requiring O(n log³ n) time, followed by a more complicated second algorithm requiring O(n log² n) time, with the O(n log² n) worst-case bound not having been improved since.\n\n### Technical Approach\n\nThe algorithm by Aggarwal and Suri used matrix searching techniques, namely for finding row minima in certain types of partial Monge matrices.\n\nThe paper was published in the 3rd Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG) in 1987.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"417c94ef-d84e-4ac7-96fb-9324fdc5c811","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:06.438Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"62e6bbaa-ad7d-48e8-8ac7-0d7d0216487f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d18d379d-5ed7-4218-874e-8b5e21144d7a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KJzkqU6cYVmQA1K55Tm1JF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D bin packing optimality proof certificate infeasibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A new branch-and-cut approach for integrated planning in ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.09468\"},{\"title\":\"On the 2D Demand Bin Packing Problem: Hardness and Approximation Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.13347v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A new upper bound 2.5545 on 2D Online Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220390453_A_new_upper_bound_25545_on_2D_Online_Bin_Packing\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithms for the Bin Packing Problem with Scenarios\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.15351\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 8 Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://ac.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/lak_teaching/ws11_12/combopt/notes/bin_packing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing.html\"},{\"title\":\"A new upper bound 2.5545 on 2D Online Bin Packing | ACM Transactions on Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2000807.2000818\"}]\n\nThe search results cover various aspects of 2D bin packing research. Here are the key findings:\n\n## 2D Bin Packing Optimality and Infeasibility Approaches\n\nThe two-dimensional bin packing problem (2D-BPP) is decomposed into a master problem and several subproblems, where the master problem is a one-dimensional BPP that assigns items to bins, and feasibility of each bin assignment is then checked in a separate two-dimensional orthogonal packing/knapsack (2D-OPP/2D-KP) subproblem.\n\n### Infeasibility Certificates and Cuts\n\nWhen an infeasible subproblem is found, a cut is added to exclude the infeasible assignment of items to bins. Improvements to the decomposition approach include cut strengthening by finding reduced infeasible sets (decrease lhs and rhs of infeasibility cuts), and cut lifting by finding valid item displacements for infeasible sets (increasing lhs while keeping rhs constant).\n\n### Proving Infeasibility Efficiently\n\nMultiple verification procedures use lower bound techniques before invoking relaxation approaches based on DFF and the non-contiguous bin packing problem (NCBP), and if infeasibility cannot be proven with these steps, the 2D-OPR is solved with a CP model.\n\n### Proving Optimality\n\nThe Positions and Covering methodology establishes a set of valid positions where each item could be placed (with pseudo-polynomial size), then fixes the total number of bins K based on the area of items divided by bin area. If the decision version of 2D-BPP is feasible for a given K, then K is the optimal value; otherwise K is increased by one and the covering model is solved again.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"03abae0e-343f-4b0f-b40c-de5eb2e04b22","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:08.042Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d18d379d-5ed7-4218-874e-8b5e21144d7a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
