{"parentUuid":"c674508d-93c6-4c1a-b680-a2ff9197c28d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NHkk1WrJFdCc5LYgi579Dd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WqdvAA7nu2zYsq3ZReYjyh","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"SoCG 2024 SoCG 2026 maximal empty rectangle algorithm survey"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1531,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6084,"cache_read_input_tokens":28765,"output_tokens":226,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6084},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1531,"output_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":28765,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6084,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy9TAJDWR9obdQpuVvS","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec194872-f0ea-4ae8-903a-5bcb298dac25","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:45.171Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ec194872-f0ea-4ae8-903a-5bcb298dac25","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WqdvAA7nu2zYsq3ZReYjyh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SoCG 2024 SoCG 2026 maximal empty rectangle algorithm survey\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes Timothy M. Chan !\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol189-socg2021/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SoCG 2026 - CG Week 2026 - Computational Geometry\",\"url\":\"https://cgweek26.computational-geometry.org/contribute/\"},{\"title\":\"SoCG: Symposium on Computational Geometry 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=2722\"},{\"title\":\"Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://socg25.github.io/socg.html\"},{\"title\":\"CGWeek 2024\",\"url\":\"https://socg24.athenarc.gr/socg.html\"},{\"title\":\"SoCG 2024\",\"url\":\"https://socg24.hotcrp.com/\"},{\"title\":\"An Optimal Algorithm for Computing Many Faces in Line ArrangementsA preliminary version of this paper will appear in Proceedings of the 42nd International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2026).\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.04863\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Geometry\",\"url\":\"https://www.computational-geometry.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Fast algorithms for computing the largest empty rectangle | Proceedings of the third annual symposium on Computational geometry\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/41958.41988\"},{\"title\":\"SoCG 2026\",\"url\":\"https://socg26.hotcrp.com/\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found relevant information about the computational geometry conferences and research on empty rectangles:\n\n## SoCG 2024 and 2026\n\nThe 40th International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2024) was held in Athens, Greece, June 11–14, 2024, while SoCG 2026 is the 42nd International Symposium on Computational Geometry.\n\n## Maximal Empty Rectangle Algorithm\n\nRegarding research on empty rectangles, the search results show that this is an established area of computational geometry research. The largest empty rectangle problem involves finding the largest rectangle B ⊂ B0 such that B does not contain any points of P in its interior, given a set P of n points in the plane and a fixed rectangle B0. \n\nAggarwal and Suri presented an algorithm at SoCG'87 requiring O(n log³ n) time, followed by a more complicated second algorithm requiring O(n log² n) time.\n\nHowever, I did not find a specific survey paper on maximal empty rectangle algorithms that was published at SoCG 2024 or accepted for SoCG 2026 in these search results. If you're looking for a specific paper on this topic, you may want to check the official conference proceedings or submission sites directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"37926f07-3b3f-4b28-b242-65ab5e946e57","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:51.397Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ec194872-f0ea-4ae8-903a-5bcb298dac25","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c674508d-93c6-4c1a-b680-a2ff9197c28d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018YGpbfXMEergdTdx2TFa7v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"hierarchical rectangle packing\" multi-level Benders 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2512.20239] Hierarchical Rectangle Packing Solved by Multi-Level Recursive Logic-based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.20239\"},{\"title\":\"Hierarchical Rectangle Packing Solved by Multi-Level Recursive Logic-based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.20239\"},{\"title\":\"Hierarchical Rectangle Packing Solved by Multi-Level Recursive Logic-based Benders Decomposition | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/arxiv/2512.20239\"},{\"title\":\"A Primal Decomposition Algorithm for the Two-dimensional ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.06835\"},{\"title\":\"Contents lists available at ScienceDirect Journal of Manufacturing Systems\",\"url\":\"https://eprints.sztaki.hu/10802/1/Dobrovoczki_384_35454253_ny.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Scheduling-based Constraint Programming Approach to Solving a\",\"url\":\"https://tidel.mie.utoronto.ca/pubs/Theses/Luo_Yiqing_202208_MASc_thesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Solving-the-PPSP-and-the-BPP-with-contiguity-constraints-2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical Models and Decomposition Algorithms for ...\",\"url\":\"https://files.core.ac.uk/download/pdf/84348559.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Model-based Decomposition Algorithms for Complex Routing ...\",\"url\":\"https://tidel.mie.utoronto.ca/pubs/Theses/Zhang_Jiachen_202510_PhD_thesis.pdf\"}]\n\nI found highly relevant results on your query. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Hierarchical Rectangle Packing with Multi-Level Benders Decomposition (2025)\n\nA recent paper (2512.20239) studies the two-dimensional hierarchical rectangle packing problem, motivated by applications in analog integrated circuit layout, facility layout, and logistics. Unlike classical strip or bin packing, the dimensions of the container are not fixed, and the packing is inherently hierarchical: each item is either a rectangle or a block occurrence, whose dimensions are a solution of another packing problem.\n\n### Key Methodological Contributions\n\nThe paper introduces a novel multilevel Logic-based Benders Decomposition method, which is a heuristic method that dynamically refines block dimension constraints, eliminating the need for manual selection of candidate widths or aspect ratios.\n\nThe authors formally define the problem and propose exact formulations in Mixed-Integer Linear Programming and Constraint Programming, but given the computational difficulty of solving complex packing instances directly, they propose decomposition heuristics.\n\n### Approach and Results\n\nThe work first implements an existing Bottom-Up baseline method that solves subblocks before combining them at higher levels. Experiments on synthetic instances with up to seven hierarchy levels, 80 items per block, and limited computation time show that the proposed decomposition significantly outperforms both monolithic formulations and the Bottom-Up method in terms of solution quality and scalability.\n\nThe paper was published in December 2025 on arXiv (ID: 2512.20239).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"77dbaee5-27be-4a84-8316-9165b9a73cbf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:52.710Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c674508d-93c6-4c1a-b680-a2ff9197c28d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"77dbaee5-27be-4a84-8316-9165b9a73cbf","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad71ee75d5a04187e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017GrTDSoaVrMrWQtY1iDzWg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me now synthesize the report.\n\n---\n\n# 学术界对 2D placement / 最大空白矩形 / packing 类问题\"手工证明最优\"的调研\n\n## 1. Maximum Empty Rectangle 经典工作脉络\n\n学术上 MER（点集中最大空白矩形）和我们的问题**形式相似但目标完全不同**：他们求的是\"给定点集，找最大空白轴向矩形\"，复杂度从 Naamad/Lee/Hsu (1984) 的 O(n²)，到 Chazelle/Drysdale/Lee (1986) 的 O(n log³ n)，到 Aggarwal/Suri SoCG'87 的 O(n log² n)，再到 Chan SoCG 2021 的 O(n α(n) log n)。这条线**全是算法复杂度推进**，没有针对单个 instance 的\"手工最优证明\"——他们追求的是通用算法，instance 是输入而非证明对象。\n\n借鉴价值：**有限**。MER 处理\"点障碍\"，我们处理\"矩形障碍 + 必须放置 266 实例 + 端口绑定 + 路由\"，约束维度差太多。但 Chan 2021 用的 staircase decomposition 思路（把搜索空间按\"L 形拐角\"分块）和我们 ghost rectangle 的子矩形枚举有点共鸣，可以参考其分解结构。\n\n## 2. 网格 placement 最优性证明\n\n真正贴近我们问题的是 **2D Orthogonal Packing / Bin Packing 的 exact 文献**：\n\n- **Clautiaux/Carlier/Moukrim/Jouglet** 系列（2007-2008）：用 logic-based Benders（LBBD）解 2D-OPP，master 用面积松弛，subproblem 检查几何放置可行性，infeasibility 通过 **exponentially many no-good cuts** 表达。关键洞察：no-good cuts 应该对应**最小不可行子集（Minimal Infeasible Subset, MIS）**，否则 cut 太弱、收敛太慢。\n- **Korf** ICAPS 2003/2004 + AIJ 2010：optimal rectangle packing，用 anytime branch-and-bound + **wasted-space lower bound**（把 2D 松弛成 1D bin packing）+ **dominance based on empty strips**（连续空条带的支配条件）。在 n=16 上加速 12000 倍。\n- **Hougardy** 系列：scale-invariant perfect packing。\n- **arXiv 2512.20239 (Dec 2025)** \"Hierarchical Rectangle Packing Solved by Multi-Level Recursive LBBD\"：**直接对应我们的 master/binding/routing/flow 多层 Benders 架构**，做 IC layout 和 facility layout 应用，提出\"动态精炼 block 维度约束\"代替手工候选枚举——这篇值得细读。\n\n## 3. SoCG 2024-2026\n\nSoCG 2024-2026 主流是几何算法复杂度（line arrangements、3D knapsack approximation 等），**没有看到针对具体大型 instance 的手工 INFEASIBLE 证明工作**。学术圈的范式是\"通用算法 + 复杂度证明\"，不是\"specific instance + handcrafted proof\"。\n\n## 4. 玩家社区/数学竞赛证明\n\n- **Factorio/Satisfactory 社区**：大量 throughput 优化讨论，但**没有形式化最优证明**——他们追求 ratio 平衡和实用 layout，不证 max 面积。\n- **数学竞赛传统（polyomino tiling impossibility）**：这条线**反而最有借鉴价值**。MOP 2007 Yufei Zhao 的 Tiling 笔记、MDPI 2022 \"A New Algorithm Based on Colouring Arguments\"、INTEGERS 2023 \"Coloring and Boundary Invariants for Polyominoes\" 系统化了**着色论证（coloring/parity argument）**——把 2D 不可行性归约到 1D 线性丢番图方程的 parity violation 上。Mutilated chessboard 是经典：去掉对角两格，31 个 domino 必覆盖 31 黑 31 白，但实际是 32 黑 30 白，矛盾。\n- **DFF（Dual Feasible Functions）**（Clautiaux/Moukrim/Carvalho）：实质是着色论证的**连续松弛形式**——把每个 item 的\"权重\"通过单调超可加函数变换，求和得到下界证书。是学术化、可计算化的\"高级着色\"。\n\n## 5. 这些技巧能否转 CP-SAT cut\n\n可以，且很值得：\n\n1. **MIS-based no-good cuts**：当 binding/routing subproblem 报 INFEASIBLE 时，不要把整个 master 解 ban 掉，而是先找最小不可行子集（drop-by-drop or QuickXplain），再 ban。我们当前 cut 强度可能偏弱。\n2. **DFF 下界 + 着色论证**：在 ghost rectangle 上预计算 DFF 下界，可以**在 master 阶段就证明某些 (W,H) 不可能装下 266 实例**，无需进入 binding/routing。这是廉价的 area-based pruning 升级版。\n3. **Empty-strip dominance（Korf）**：如果 ghost rectangle 边缘存在长度 ≥ k 的连续空条带且没有任何端口或必要设施在其投影内，则该 layout 被支配，可加 dominance cut。\n4. **Coloring parity**：266 实例的端口位置如果带有 mod-k 不变量（例如 power pole 必须每 7 格一个），可以用着色论证证明某些坐标余数下端口需求不可能被满足，转成 master 上的线性约束。\n5. **多层 LBBD 经验（2512.20239）**：动态精炼 block 维度约束的思路可以套到我们 ghost rectangle 候选上——不要预生成全部 (W,H) 候选，让 master 反馈来收紧。\n\n## 对我们 cut 设计有没有可借鉴\n\n**有，且强烈建议补做三件事**：\n\n1. 把 binding/routing 失败时的 no-good cut 从\"整解 ban\"升级到 **MIS-based**（Clautiaux 路线，已有成熟算法），预计能让 Benders 收敛速度提升一个量级。\n2. 在 master 层加 **DFF lower bound** 作为 area-based pruning 的强化版，廉价地排除大批 (W,H) 候选，无需调用 subproblem。\n3. 阅读 arXiv 2512.20239（Dec 2025），它的 multi-level recursive LBBD 架构和我们 master/binding/routing/flow 几乎同构，里面的 cut 强化和动态精炼技巧可能可以直接迁移。\n\n至于\"针对具体 instance 的手工 INFEASIBLE 证明\"——**学术界基本不做这种工作**，他们追求通用算法。我们项目要做的 certified_exact 在学术上偏冷门（因为它本质是单 instance 的工业级 proof），但**底层 cut 技术全是有学术依据的**，没必要从零设计。\n\n## 关键参考链接\n\nSources:\n- [Largest empty rectangle - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largest_empty_rectangle)\n- [Naamad, Lee, Hsu 1984 - On the maximum empty rectangle problem](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0166218X84901240)\n- [Chan SoCG 2021 - Faster Algorithms for Largest Empty Rectangles and Boxes](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol189-socg2021/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.24.pdf)\n- [Aggarwal & Suri SoCG'87](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/41958.41988)\n- [Hierarchical Rectangle Packing by Multi-Level Recursive LBBD (Dec 2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.20239)\n- [Korf ICAPS 2003 - Optimal Rectangle Packing: Initial Results](https://cdn.aaai.org/ICAPS/2003/ICAPS03-029.pdf)\n- [Korf ICAPS 2004 - New Results](https://icaps04.icaps-conference.org/icapspapers/ICAPS04KorfR.pdf)\n- [Clautiaux/Carlier - A new exact method for 2D orthogonal packing](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-new-exact-method-for-the-two-dimensional-packing-Clautiaux-Carlier/f7d5f8c60972c18812925715f685ce8ae5d5659d)\n- [Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening in LBBD](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3)\n- [Hooker - Logic-based Benders Decomposition for Large-scale Optimization](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf)\n- [BinPacking2D GitHub - exact branch-and-cut](https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D)\n- [Dual-feasible functions for 2D bin packing (Clautiaux/Moukrim)](https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207540802426656)\n- [MDPI 2022 - Colouring Arguments for Identifying Impossible Polyomino Tilings](https://www.mdpi.com/1999-4893/15/2/65)\n- [Yufei Zhao MOP 2007 - Tiling: Coloring and Weights](https://yufeizhao.com/olympiad/tiling.pdf)\n- [INTEGERS 2023 - Coloring and Boundary Invariants for Polyominoes](https://math.colgate.edu/~integers/x73/x73.pdf)\n- [Mutilated chessboard problem - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutilated_chessboard_problem)\n- [Positions and Covering for 2D-BPP](https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1111,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3128,"cache_read_input_tokens":34849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3128,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyAN31JU68SV969ocdg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6395cab-2ba2-4985-a410-53abad39da67","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:57.638Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
